1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:13,393
By the eleventh morning, three cities had offered me keys, two had
offered me houses, and one had asked whether I would consider becoming
its most famous resident without technically having to live there.

2
00:00:13,643 --> 00:00:34,671
"Nigga," Tank said, looking at the envelopes, "they recruiting you
like weather." We sat in the palace breakfast room with the sea beyond
the windows and eight white ships still trying to make a horizon
threatening. My people had spread across every comfortable chair.
Mercedes read the Velvet Mile paperwork with Porsche.

3
00:00:34,921 --> 00:00:56,755
Rosa wrote wedding ideas on the back of a menu and crossed out every
place that wasn't Vegas because Tank said if he was going to cry in
front of a whole city, he wanted a city that already knew him. Shawna
sat beside me with her feet in my lap. I opened the first envelope.
Port Carmine wanted to name its waterfront after me.

4
00:00:57,005 --> 00:01:14,467
Gilded Bay wanted a photograph of me holding its rescue-service flag.
San Paloma wanted to know whether I would attend the opening of a
sports arena built by a man whose nephew had been on the ferry. "Tell
them yes," I said. "To all?" Shawna asked.

5
00:01:14,717 --> 00:01:32,329
"Nigga, I got a calendar." "You have me reminding you what day it is."
"Premium calendar." She pinched my knee. Then Vegas called. One of my
westside managers, a man named Boone who had never met a dollar he
couldn't persuade into staying overnight.

6
00:01:32,579 --> 00:01:50,164
He told me the clubs were full, the new cars had arrived, and two
niggas had tried telling him my absence meant their debts had become
historical. "History got interest," I said. "That's what I told them."
"No trouble at Shawna's property. No touching the staff.

7
00:01:50,414 --> 00:02:07,956
And if a nigga says my badge made me forget my money, show him the
part where I'm still asking about it." Knox looked up from her coffee.
I looked back. She took another sip. Nigga, we understood each other.
I wasn't going home to become a decorative good man.

8
00:02:08,206 --> 00:02:33,076
I had built an empire full of cash, cars, vice, and people who knew
which door to knock on when their own night got complicated. The badge
had given my jacket another beautiful place to shine. It had not
turned the rest of me into a church bulletin. By noon the visiting
dignitaries arrived carrying velvet boxes. No speeches about policy.
Thank God.

9
00:02:33,326 --> 00:02:53,281
These people had seen enough of my week to know a nigga should not be
trapped behind a podium if anything with an engine remained nearby.
The woman from Port Carmine handed me a gold key shaped like a fish.
"Our harbor," she said. The man from Gilded Bay gave me a silver key
shaped like a wing.

10
00:02:53,531 --> 00:03:18,617
"Our sky." San Paloma gave me a key that looked almost normal until I
realized it had my face engraved on the teeth. Tank leaned close.
"Nigga, you can unlock your own mouth." I nearly ruined the photograph
laughing. Then Shawna received a key too. Blue enamel. A little treble
clef worked into the handle. The woman from Port Carmine presented it
with both hands.

11
00:03:18,867 --> 00:03:39,785
"For the hall where we want you to sing," she said. My wife stared at
it. I watched her thumb move over the blue enamel. The crowd waited,
cameras raised, but she took one small second for herself before
smiling. "I'd like that," she said. Nigga, I would have bought that
whole harbor for the way she looked at the key.

12
00:03:40,035 --> 00:03:56,466
But somebody else had heard her and wanted her there. I couldn't
improve that by reaching for money. So I stood beside her, proud
enough to hurt, and let the room give my wife something she had made
happen herself. The parade afterward was less restrained.

13
00:03:56,716 --> 00:04:20,877
Cassius and Inez brought the Monaco prize cars out in a line of color
so bright the street looked wet. Red, white, silver, gold, my dark-
blue Lamborghini leading them with its repaired side reflecting the
crowd. Mechanics had fixed the scrape while I slept. The chief's gold
shield was clean again. Nigga looked rested even when I wasn't.

14
00:04:21,127 --> 00:04:44,837
Mercedes drove a green convertible with Porsche beside her, both
wearing scarves like the wind had been hired specifically to flatter
them. Darius and Kong rode in a car too small for either man's pride,
their knees practically in the windshield. Tank drove Rosa in the old
black Mercedes because he said some cars earned the right to carry the
good part too.

15
00:04:45,087 --> 00:05:05,324
I rode with Shawna. We passed the market. Passed Alma's kitchens.
Passed the repaired ferry dock where the man I'd pulled from the water
stood beside his husband holding a sign that said THE CAPTAIN CAME
BACK. Shawna touched my arm when she saw it. I lifted my hand to them.
The whole street answered.

16
00:05:05,574 --> 00:05:30,648
At the top of the hill, an armored car burst out of a side road and
struck the lead escort. The celebration broke apart. Another car came
behind it. Then a third. Black paint. Covered plates. Saint's men had
stopped wearing visible crests after Porsche made the joke, but a
nigga doesn't become mysterious by changing his laundry after
everybody has seen his face.

17
00:05:30,898 --> 00:05:55,374
Shots cracked across the road. I pulled Shawna low and turned the
Lamborghini between the attackers and the crowd. Cassius swung his red
car across the opposite lane. Inez came up behind him, trapping the
first armored car between two machines whose owners had already beaten
an entire continent at driving. The attacker's driver tried to force
his way through.

18
00:05:55,624 --> 00:06:11,685
Cassius smiled at him through the windshield. Nigga, that smile meant
a repair bill was about to become a biography. I took the second car
up the hill away from the spectators. It followed, gunfire chipping
the wall beside us.

19
00:06:11,935 --> 00:06:30,124
Shawna held the radio in one hand and my spare magazine in the other,
her face calm, her voice telling the captains exactly where the people
needed space. "Left at the fountain," she said. "I see it." "The lower
road's clear." "I see that too." "Aiden." I glanced at her.

20
00:06:30,375 --> 00:06:45,057
"I am enjoying this less than you." "Baby, I can enjoy enough for both
of us." She laughed despite the gunfire, and I took the turn. The
armored car came after us too fast. Its weight dragged it wide.

21
00:06:45,307 --> 00:07:03,449
I went around the fountain, crossed the little stone square, and came
back against its flank while the driver still tried to persuade
physics to consider his rank. We struck hard enough to fold its front
wheel under the body. The car stopped in the fountain. Water climbed
over the hood.

22
00:07:03,699 --> 00:07:17,806
For one beautiful second every statue in the square appeared to be
spitting on the nigga simultaneously. I stepped out with my gun up.
"Everybody out." The driver opened his door into waist-deep water.

23
00:07:18,056 --> 00:07:42,257
"Nigga," I said, "you picked a dramatic place to park." Behind us,
Tank had stopped the third car by putting the old Mercedes across its
path and letting Darius and Kong emerge from the tiny convertible
together. The gunmen looked at the two enormous men. One put his
weapon on the dashboard before either fighter spoke. "Intelligent
nigga," Tank said.

24
00:07:42,507 --> 00:08:06,698
The first armored car belonged to Cassius and Inez now, in the sense
that neither of them intended to permit it another decision. Its
driver came out holding both hands over his head and asking which
champion was arresting him. "All of them," Knox said, arriving with
the island police. No spectator had been hit. One escort officer had a
broken wrist.

25
00:08:06,948 --> 00:08:33,177
Two attackers were wounded. The fountain needed a new statue hand. My
Lamborghini's new paint had lasted approximately forty-seven minutes.
Shawna looked at the fresh scrape. "You couldn't keep one side
pretty?" "Baby, I'm keeping both our sides alive. The car understands
the priorities." From the stalled armored car, a phone began ringing.
I answered on video. Saint's face filled the screen.

26
00:08:33,427 --> 00:08:56,049
He saw the fountain behind me. His eyes closed briefly. "Nigga," I
said, "you should stop buying these cars if you're going to keep
giving them to my city." He opened his eyes. "Tomorrow. The final
challenge. No more proxies. You and me." "I been here." "At dawn, the
twenty champions ride. By noon, one reaches the Crown Gate.

27
00:08:56,299 --> 00:09:20,984
I will be waiting." "Wear the necklace." His hand moved to the Lion's
Heart beneath his collar. "Earn it." I ended the call before he could
enjoy saying anything else. The visiting officials stood at the edge
of the square, velvet key boxes still under their arms. They had
watched the whole thing. Their escorts had watched it. Their
photographers had photographed every expensive second.

28
00:09:21,234 --> 00:09:35,632
The woman from Port Carmine looked at the car in the fountain. Then at
my wife. Then at me. "We should give you a bigger key," she said. Tank
bent over laughing. Nigga, every city really did want me.
